.Dd October 7, 2026
.Dt TPOSD 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm tposd
.Nd on-screen display for ThinkPad brightness and mute keys
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl n
.Op Fl i Ar interval
.Nm
.Cm brightness
.Sm off
.Op Cm + | Cm \-
.Ar N
.Sm on
.Nm
.Cm pcm
.Sm off
.Op Cm + | Cm \-
.Ar N
.Sm on
.Nm
.Cm micmute
.Op Cm on | off | toggle
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Without a command,
.Nm
watches the screen brightness, the speaker mute of the ThinkPad embedded
controller and the microphone mute, and shows a desktop notification
whenever one of them changes, whoever changed it.
It is started with the desktop session by
.Pa @PREFIX@/etc/xdg/autostart/tposd.desktop .
.Pp
It reads:
.Bl -tag -width "microphone mute"
.It brightness
.Pa /dev/backlight/backlight0 ,
see
.Xr backlight 9 .
The notification has a bar.
.It speaker mute
the sysctl
.Va dev.acpi_ibm.0.mute ,
see
.Xr acpi_ibm 4 .
The embedded controller mutes the speaker in hardware when the mute key is
pressed, and sends no event.
.Nm
turns the mute LED on and off, which
.Xr acpi_ibm 4
does not.
.It microphone mute
the recording level
.Pq Dq rec
of every mixer that has one, see
.Xr mixer 3 .
A laptop's internal microphone is often a sound device of its own, so all
of them are muted together; the microphone counts as muted when all are.
.Nm
keeps the microphone mute LED in step with it.
.El
.Pp
At start and on every change of the speaker or microphone mute,
.Nm
sets the mute LEDs with
.Xr tposd-mute-led 8
through
.Xr pkexec 1 .
If that fails, it warns once and goes on.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl i Ar interval
Poll every
.Ar interval
milliseconds, 50 to 60000 (default 200).
.It Fl n
Do not set the mute LEDs.
.El
.Pp
The commands are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm brightness Oo Cm + | Cm \- Oc Ns Ar N
Change the screen brightness by
.Ar N
percent, or set it to
.Ar N
percent without a sign, and print the new value.
Bind the brightness keys to
.Ql tposd brightness +10
and
.Ql tposd brightness -10 .
.It Cm pcm Oo Cm + | Cm \- Oc Ns Ar N
The same for the OSS
.Dq pcm
level of the default mixer, which PulseAudio does not reliably manage.
.It Cm micmute Op Cm on | off | toggle
Mute
.Pq Cm on
or unmute
.Pq Cm off
the microphone, or toggle it, and print the new state,
.Dq on
or
.Dq off .
Without an argument, only print it.
The mute LED follows through the watcher, or through
.Pa @LIBEXECDIR@/tposd-key
for the mic-mute key.
.El
.Pp
The watcher logs to
.Xr syslog 3
with the identifier
.Dq tposd :
a failing
.Xr pkexec 1 ,
a failing notification, and, at start, when the kernel can not read the
environment of the process
.Pq Va kern.proc.env ,
which keeps ConsoleKit and so polkit from finding the session.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Pa @PREFIX@/etc/devd/tposd.conf
.Xr devd 8
rule for the microphone mute key, which arrives only as an ACPI event.
.It Pa @LIBEXECDIR@/tposd-key
run by this rule as root: runs
.Ql tposd micmute toggle
and sets the LED.
.It Pa @PREFIX@/lib/xfce4/panel/plugins/libtposd-panel.so
the XFCE panel plugin
.Dq ThinkPad Controls .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Make the screen darker by 10 percent:
.Dl $ tposd brightness -10
.Pp
Set the OSS pcm level to 100 percent:
.Dl $ tposd pcm 100
.Pp
See the messages of the watcher:
.Dl $ grep tposd /var/log/messages
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pkexec 1 ,
.Xr mixer 3 ,
.Xr syslog 3 ,
.Xr acpi_ibm 4 ,
.Xr devd 8 ,
.Xr mixer 8 ,
.Xr tposd-mute-led 8 ,
.Xr tposd-setup 8 ,
.Xr backlight 9
.Sh AUTHORS
.An wugq Aq Mt wugq.dev@gmail.com
